# Digital Wallet Backend

Backend application for managing digital wallet accounts and user operations.  
Built using Spring Boot, PostgreSQL, and Docker.

---

## Tech Stack

- Java 21
- Spring Boot
- Spring Data JPA
- Hibernate
- PostgreSQL
- Docker
- Maven
- REST API
- Linux

---

## Features

- REST API for managing users and wallets
- Create and retrieve wallet accounts
- Database integration using PostgreSQL
- Entity relationships using JPA and Hibernate
- Layered architecture (Controller, Service, Repository)
- Exception handling with proper HTTP responses
- Docker container support

---

## Architecture

Project uses standard backend layered architecture:

```
Controller → Service → Repository → Database
```

- Controller — handles HTTP requests
- Service — business logic
- Repository — database access
- Entity — database models

---

## Example Endpoints

```
GET     /api/users
POST    /api/users

GET     /api/wallets
POST    /api/wallets
```

---

## How to Run

### Run locally

Requirements:

- Java 21+
- PostgreSQL
- Maven

```
git clone https://github.com/kqwakrss/digital-wallet-backend.git
cd digital-wallet-backend
./mvnw spring-boot:run
```

---

### Run with Docker

```
docker build -t digital-wallet-backend .
docker run -p 8080:8080 digital-wallet-backend
```

